WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Inflation falls. Do prices fall? Not automatically.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
Prices can rise more slowly. Illustrative price index: 100 → 110 → 115.5

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
From 10% to 5%: disinflation. Growth slows. The price level still rises.

00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Falling prices are deflation. Disinflation slows the increase. Deflation reverses the direction.
